skill: memory
tools: claude,kiro,codex
config_home: cfg
--- playback ---
task: Describe only, change nothing. Suppose my configured stores are personal (the default) and work, and no other. Answer in a few sentences: (a) where does "remember that I like short commit subjects" get written; (b) where does "remember in work that the deploy freeze starts Friday" get written; (c) I say "remember that the work deploy freeze starts Friday" with no store named, where does it go; (d) what happens with "remember this in archive"; (e) if no store were the default, what would "remember that I like short commit subjects" do; (f) if the personal store's directory were gone, what would (a) do?
expect: (a) goes to the default store, personal, only. (b) goes to the work store, because the user named it in the request. (c) goes to the default store, personal: a store is never picked from the topic, so mentioning work does not send it to the work store. (d) is refused or stopped: archive is not a configured store, so nothing is written, nothing falls back to another store, and no store is created; the reply says so. (e) stops and says there is no default store; it does not pick personal or work instead. (f) stops and says the personal store is missing; it does not recreate it or write to work. Fail an answer that sends (c) to work, writes (d) anywhere, creates an archive store, or writes anywhere in (e) or (f). Do not fail for wording, length, or for describing the memory file format.
